transition-duration and animation-duration: duration-list longhands, read as transition-delay and animation-delay are.
'auto' (the initial value) keeps the durations the shorthand's list declares; a declared list replaces them item by item;
a duration is a time that is not negative (0s is valid). The PAL follows each transition or animation shorthand with
its longhands' 'auto', as a CSS shorthand resets its longhands.
CSS Transitions 1: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-transitions-1/#transition-duration-property
CSS Animations 1: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-animations-1/#animation-duration

